  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Thursday)\nIssued at 208 PM MDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery shows broad upper ridging centered across south \nSE CONUS with the main axis stretching through the Midwest. Moist, \nactive southwesterly flow continues across the western CONUS...all \nthe way back to a trough near the West Coast. Several shortwaves \nare crossing northern High Plains to the central/northern \nRockies. The nearest wave is pushing through central/eastern WY \nthrough the NE WY zones south into the CYS CWA. As the wave \ncontinues NE, showers and thunderstorms will push further into \nwestern SD while weakening. Weak CAPE and shear will damper any \nsevere weather potential today. The next (much stronger) wave will\nbring continued chances of elevated convection late this evening \nand into the overnight hours. These showers could generally \nproduce up to half an inch of QPF by 12z. Active weather will \ncontinue through Friday with additional shortwaves bringing \nmid-level forcing. Models show a surface low strengthening \ntomorrow near the ND/MT line with a cold front pushing through NE\nWY and far western SD. Good Theta E advection across NW/Central \nSD ahead of the front will support SBCAPE nearing 2000 J/kg. While\nshear is not impressive, could still see pulsing isolated \nstrong/severe storms Friday afternoon and early evening, with \nlarge hail as the main threat. Active weather and near average \ntemperatures will continue through weekend into the first half of \nnext week, with daily chances for showers and thunderstorms.",
